+---
+title: "Contact Nixflex support and follow your ticket"
+sidebarTitle: "Contact support"
+description: "Choose a request type in Help, ask for a higher simultaneous call limit, and find the latest public reply in your dashboard or the Nixflex phone app."
+canonical: "https://docs.nixflex.com/guides/business/support-tickets"
+---
+
+Use a ticket to keep the request and replies together. If you prefer email, write to [support@nixflex.com](mailto:support@nixflex.com). We aim to reply within 48 hours, including weekends.
+
+## Send a request
+
+1. Sign in to the organisation the request is about. In the dashboard open **Settings → Help**. In the phone app open **Account → Help**.
+2. Under **Contact us**, check your name, business and verified email. These fields come from your account. If you have no verified email, you can still use **My tickets**.
+3. Choose the request type and write a message. Include the time and what you were trying to do. Leave out passwords, keys and private call content. Your first nonblank line becomes the subject.
+4. Choose **Send request**. If the outcome is unclear, let Help check the original request. If your workspace changed, reopen Help in the intended account and check **My tickets** before starting again.
+
+| Choose | What to include |
+| --- | --- |
+| Increase my simultaneous call limit | The total number of calls you need at one time and why. Support reviews the request before a limit changes. |
+| Complaint or problem | What happened, when and what you expected. Use this for a billing problem too. |
+| Report abuse | What happened and when, with a safe reference if you have one. |
+| Other | What you need help with. |
+
+## Follow the conversation
+
+Open **My tickets**. Check the type, date opened, status and latest public reply. Select a subject to see its messages. Owners and Admins can read the organisation’s tickets. A Member sees the tickets they personally opened while they still have access.
+
+**Waiting for your reply** means support needs something from you. Send your reply in the thread. Choose **Mark done** once the issue is resolved. If it comes back, reply to reopen it. If someone updated the ticket while you were writing, refresh it and read their reply first. A notification email directs you back to sign in and read the conversation.
+
+## Common questions
+
+**Can I ask for a call back?** The form offers the four choices above. Older callback tickets remain in your history.
+
+**Can I check a ticket on my phone?** In the app, **Account → Help** includes the request form and ticket list. **Copy email address** lets you use your own mail app.
+
+**Does a request immediately increase my call limit?** Your current limit applies until a reviewed change is confirmed.
+
+[Account settings](/guides/business/account) · [Support for developers](/guides/developer/support-tickets)
