+---
+title: "Open and recover support tickets with the Nixflex API"
+sidebarTitle: "Support tickets in code"
+description: "Create a ticket, read its public thread, reply at the latest version, and recover a personal request in the same workspace after a lost response."
+canonical: "https://docs.nixflex.com/guides/developer/support-tickets"
+---
+
+Use a server-side organisation key to work with the organisation’s tickets. A personal bearer session has the signed-in person’s current access and MFA requirements. Members can work with their own tickets. Keep ticket text private.
+
+## 1. Find the ticket
+
+<CodeGroup>
+
+```bash cURL
+curl "https://api.nixflex.com/v1/support/tickets?limit=5" -H "Authorization: Bearer $NIXFLEX_API_KEY"
+```
+
+```javascript Node
+const response = await fetch('https://api.nixflex.com/v1/support/tickets?limit=5', {
+  headers: { Authorization: 'Bearer ' + process.env.NIXFLEX_API_KEY }
+})
+if (!response.ok) throw new Error('HTTP ' + response.status)
+const page = await response.json()
+```
+
+```python Python
+import json, os, urllib.request
+req = urllib.request.Request('https://api.nixflex.com/v1/support/tickets?limit=5',
+    headers={'Authorization': 'Bearer ' + os.environ['NIXFLEX_API_KEY']})
+with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=15) as response:
+    page = json.load(response)
+```
+
+```powershell PowerShell
+$headers = @{ Authorization = "Bearer $env:NIXFLEX_API_KEY" }
+$page = Invoke-RestMethod -Uri 'https://api.nixflex.com/v1/support/tickets?limit=5' -Headers $headers
+```
+
+</CodeGroup>
+
+An empty page is `{"tickets":[],"next_cursor":null}`. Preserve the filters and pass any returned cursor back unchanged. Read the individual ticket to obtain its current version and public conversation.
+
+## 2. Submit once in the intended workspace
+
+Choose a unique `Idempotency-Key` for each intended create, reply or solve. Keep the key with the exact action, body and revision. For a personal create or reply, capture the workspace’s public `key_id` **when the draft starts** and send it in `X-Nixflex-Expected-Account`. Never derive that header from whichever workspace happens to be open when retrying. An organisation key already selects its workspace.
+
+[Create](/api-reference/support/create) uses `message`. [Reply](/api-reference/support/reply) uses `body` and the thread’s latest version in `X-Expected-Revision`. [Mark done](/api-reference/support/solve) takes that version in the JSON body. A reply can reopen a solved ticket.
+
+## 3. Recover a lost acknowledgement
+
+For a personal submission, [look up the receipt](/api-reference/support/receipt) with the original signed-in person, request key and workspace header. On 200, show the current ticket and the original receipt. An organisation-key client can replay the identical write with its original key. Only an already committed and still authorised personal write can replay without the workspace header.
+
+| Result | What to do |
+| --- | --- |
+| 404 `request_not_found` | Check identity, workspace and original key. If still in doubt, refresh the list. Reuse the original key and exact payload for a deliberate retry. |
+| 409 `account_changed` | Discard the stale draft, refresh the signed-in workspace and check the intended workspace separately. Never replay the draft into the newly selected account. |
+| 409 `ticket_changed` | Read the thread. Review the new revision before composing a new change. |
+| 409 `request_conflict` | The key identifies a different payload. Reconcile the original action first. |
+| 429 or 503 | Wait and retry a read. Reconcile a write before resending. |
+
+[List tickets](/api-reference/support/list) · [Read a thread](/api-reference/support/get) · [Dashboard and app guide](/guides/business/support-tickets)
