+---
+title: "List support tickets"
+sidebarTitle: "List support tickets"
+description: "Read the tickets visible to the calling account or person and use a cursor to get the next page with the same filters."
+openapi: "/api-reference/public.openapi.json GET /support/tickets"
+playground: "simple"
+canonical: "https://docs.nixflex.com/api-reference/support/list"
+---
+
+Read the tickets visible to the calling account or person and use a cursor to get the next page with the same filters.
+
+## Access
+
+Use a server-side organisation key or a signed-in personal bearer session. Owners, Admins and organisation keys have organisation-wide ticket access. Members can access only tickets they opened.
+
+## Request fields
+
+| Field | Requirement and meaning |
+| --- | --- |
+| `limit` | Optional integer, default 20. Use 1–50. |
+| `cursor` | Optional. Use the previous `next_cursor` unchanged. Positive decimal string up to 9223372036854775807. |
+| `category` | Optional raw value: `problem`, `billing`, `raise_call_limit`, `call_me_back`, `report_abuse`, `other`. Historical values can still be filtered. |
+| `status` | Optional: `open`, `waiting_on_customer`, `solved`. |
+
+Send no request body.
+
+## Example request
+
+```bash
+curl -X GET "https://api.nixflex.com/v1/support/tickets?limit=20" \
+  -H "Authorization: Bearer $NIXFLEX_API_KEY"
+```
+
+## Response
+
+Returns `tickets[]` and `next_cursor` (string or null). The list contains summaries only. A summary includes the ticket ID, subject, raw and display categories, status, current version and timestamps. `last_public_reply` is null or an author label and time.
+
+```json
+{
+  "tickets": [
+    {
+      "id": "a2f03f19-70b8-4bb6-9f14-3bd3eb529c01",
+      "category": "other",
+      "display_category": "other",
+      "subject": "Please check our test request",
+      "status": "open",
+      "version": 1,
+      "created_at": "2026-11-23T10:00:00Z",
+      "updated_at": "2026-11-23T10:00:00Z",
+      "solved_at": null,
+      "last_customer_reply_at": "2026-11-23T10:00:00Z",
+      "last_staff_reply_at": null,
+      "last_public_reply": null
+    }
+  ],
+  "next_cursor": null
+}
+```
+
+## Errors
+
+| HTTP | Error code | What to do |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| 400 | `invalid_ticket` | Check permitted fields, value limits, headers and revision. |
+| 401 | `unauthorized`, `invalid_token` | Supply a valid organisation key or refresh the personal session. |
+| 403 | `mfa_required`, `support_access_denied` | Complete personal verification or recheck current workspace access. |
+| 429 | `rate_limit_exceeded` | Wait for the request limit to reset. |
+| 503 | `auth_unavailable`, `support_unavailable` | Retry a read later. Reconcile any write before sending again. |
+
+## Retry
+
+Retry transient reads with bounded backoff. A later read can show newer ticket state. [Ticket workflow and recovery](/guides/developer/support-tickets).
