+---
+title: "Look up a support request receipt"
+sidebarTitle: "Look up a support request receipt"
+description: "Check a personal support request after a lost response. The lookup reads the original receipt and the current ticket without sending a message."
+openapi: "/api-reference/public.openapi.json GET /support/tickets/requests/{request_key}"
+playground: "simple"
+canonical: "https://docs.nixflex.com/api-reference/support/receipt"
+---
+
+Check a personal support request after a lost response. The lookup reads the original receipt and the current ticket without sending a message.
+
+## Access
+
+Use the original person’s current bearer session and original workspace. A teammate cannot recover another person’s receipt.
+
+## Request fields
+
+| Field | Requirement and meaning |
+| --- | --- |
+| `request_key` | Required path segment. URL-encode the original `Idempotency-Key`, 1–128 letters, digits or `._:-`. |
+| `X-Nixflex-Expected-Account` | Required header. Send the original workspace’s public `key_id` captured when the submission was composed. |
+
+Send no request body.
+
+## Example request
+
+```bash
+curl -X GET "https://api.nixflex.com/v1/support/tickets/requests/example-request-001" \
+  -H "Authorization: Bearer $NIXFLEX_PERSONAL_TOKEN" \
+  -H "X-Nixflex-Expected-Account: $ORIGINAL_ACCOUNT_ID"
+```
+
+## Response
+
+Returns the current `ticket` and original `receipt`. Their versions may differ. The lookup omits message content, private notes, history, contact destination and use case. A valid organisation API key cannot look up a personal receipt and receives the same 404 as an unknown request. A summary includes the ticket ID, subject, raw and display categories, status, current version and timestamps. `last_public_reply` is null or an author label and time. The receipt records `request_id`, `operation`, original `version` and `message_id`.
+
+```json
+{
+  "ticket": {
+    "id": "a2f03f19-70b8-4bb6-9f14-3bd3eb529c01",
+    "category": "other",
+    "display_category": "other",
+    "subject": "Please check our test request",
+    "status": "open",
+    "version": 2,
+    "created_at": "2026-11-23T10:00:00Z",
+    "updated_at": "2026-11-23T10:00:00Z",
+    "solved_at": null,
+    "last_customer_reply_at": "2026-11-23T10:00:00Z",
+    "last_staff_reply_at": null,
+    "last_public_reply": {"author_label": "You", "created_at": "2026-11-23T10:00:00Z"}
+  },
+  "receipt": {
+    "request_id": "df84c8f3-ac66-404f-b50c-b91bda2abeb3",
+    "operation": "create",
+    "version": 1,
+    "message_id": "56a3de9d-a9d9-4a7e-9d56-c5388706204b"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+## Errors
+
+| HTTP | Error code | What to do |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| 401 | `unauthorized`, `invalid_token` | Supply a valid organisation key or refresh the personal session. |
+| 403 | `mfa_required`, `support_access_denied` | Complete personal verification or recheck current workspace access. |
+| 404 | `request_not_found` | Opaque result for an absent, uncommitted or inaccessible receipt. Check the original identity and key. |
+| 409 | `account_changed` | Discard the stale personal draft. Refresh Help in the intended workspace. |
+| 429 | `rate_limit_exceeded` | Wait for the request limit to reset. |
+| 503 | `auth_unavailable`, `support_unavailable` | Retry a read later. Reconcile any write before sending again. |
+
+## Retry
+
+Retry transient reads with bounded backoff. A later read can show newer ticket state. [Ticket workflow and recovery](/guides/developer/support-tickets).
