+---
+title: "Read a support ticket"
+sidebarTitle: "Read a support ticket"
+description: "Read the public conversation and its current revision before sending a reply or marking an issue done."
+openapi: "/api-reference/public.openapi.json GET /support/tickets/{ticket_id}"
+playground: "simple"
+canonical: "https://docs.nixflex.com/api-reference/support/get"
+---
+
+Read the public conversation and its current revision before sending a reply or marking an issue done.
+
+## Access
+
+Use a server-side organisation key or a signed-in personal bearer session. Owners, Admins and organisation keys have organisation-wide ticket access. Members can access only tickets they opened.
+
+## Request fields
+
+| Field | Requirement and meaning |
+| --- | --- |
+| `ticket_id` | Required UUID in the path, for a visible ticket. |
+
+Send no request body.
+
+## Example request
+
+```bash
+curl -X GET "https://api.nixflex.com/v1/support/tickets/a2f03f19-70b8-4bb6-9f14-3bd3eb529c01" \
+  -H "Authorization: Bearer $NIXFLEX_API_KEY"
+```
+
+## Response
+
+Returns `ticket`, `messages[]` and `events[]`. Messages carry an ID, author kind and label, timestamp and plain text `body`. Events carry ID, kind and timestamp. Internal staff notes are private. The thread can include `desired_limit` and `use_case` for capacity requests and historic callback details. A summary includes the ticket ID, subject, raw and display categories, status, current version and timestamps. `last_public_reply` is null or an author label and time.
+
+```json
+{
+  "ticket": {
+    "id": "a2f03f19-70b8-4bb6-9f14-3bd3eb529c01",
+    "category": "other",
+    "display_category": "other",
+    "subject": "Please check our test request",
+    "status": "open",
+    "version": 1,
+    "created_at": "2026-11-23T10:00:00Z",
+    "updated_at": "2026-11-23T10:00:00Z",
+    "solved_at": null,
+    "last_customer_reply_at": "2026-11-23T10:00:00Z",
+    "last_staff_reply_at": null,
+    "last_public_reply": null
+  },
+  "messages": [
+    {
+      "id": "56a3de9d-a9d9-4a7e-9d56-c5388706204b",
+      "author_kind": "person",
+      "author_label": "Your team",
+      "body": "Please check our test request",
+      "created_at": "2026-11-23T10:00:00Z"
+    }
+  ],
+  "events": [
+    {
+      "id": "df84c8f3-ac66-404f-b50c-b91bda2abeb3",
+      "kind": "created",
+      "created_at": "2026-11-23T10:00:00Z"
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+## Errors
+
+| HTTP | Error code | What to do |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| 400 | `invalid_ticket` | Check permitted fields, value limits, headers and revision. |
+| 401 | `unauthorized`, `invalid_token` | Supply a valid organisation key or refresh the personal session. |
+| 403 | `mfa_required`, `support_access_denied` | Complete personal verification or recheck current workspace access. |
+| 404 | `ticket_not_found` | Check the identifier, current access and account. |
+| 429 | `rate_limit_exceeded` | Wait for the request limit to reset. |
+| 503 | `auth_unavailable`, `support_unavailable` | Retry a read later. Reconcile any write before sending again. |
+
+## Retry
+
+Retry transient reads with bounded backoff. A later read can show newer ticket state. [Ticket workflow and recovery](/guides/developer/support-tickets).
